{"requirements": [
{"id": "R-SOC", "parent": "SN-1", "value": 2.98, "unit": "%", "basis": "Gross energy is 4.9311+0.071=5.0021 MWh over the 90% window. The 4.600 MWh target plus 0.071 MWh of auxiliaries needs 84.04% of window, so 5.96% may be lost, which is 2.98% at each end."},
{"id": "R-TRIP", "parent": "SN-4", "value": 150, "unit": "ms", "basis": "Cells above 3.75 V must be disconnected within 150 ms. Budget: scan time of the longest chain x 5 scans, plus a 5 ms MCU cycle and the contactor opening time."},
{"id": "R-PRE", "parent": "SN-3", "value": 9.5, "unit": "s", "basis": "The DC bus must be ready within 10 s of the start command, and the start sequence before precharge takes 0.5 s, leaving 9.5 s."},
{"id": "R-BAL", "parent": "SN-1", "value": 75.4, "unit": "mA", "basis": "Self-discharge spread at 35 C is 1.72%/month, about 0.0573%/day of 263.2 Ah, or 0.151 Ah/day. Balancing runs 2 h/day, so the current is 0.151/2 = 75.4 mA."},
{"id": "R-BRK", "parent": "SN-4", "value": 945, "unit": "A", "basis": "The 250 A gBat fuse alone protects the cell only above about 945 A (about 3.0 C), where its pre-arcing time drops below the cell short-time limit. Below that the contactor must break the current."},
{"id": "R-RIDE", "parent": "SN-6", "value": 2.04, "unit": "s", "basis": "The voltage stays below 50% from t=0 until the second recovery crosses 50% at 1.0+1.0588=2.059 s. The supply's own 20 ms hold-up is subtracted, leaving 2.04 s."},
{"id": "R-IMD", "parent": ["SN-4", "SN-6"], "value": 149.2, "unit": "uF", "basis": "All racks and PCS are galvanically joined in one IT network, so a single IMD is allowed. Capacitance: 19x1.52 + 4x30 + 19x40x2x0.19 nF = 28.88+120+0.29 = 149.2 uF."}
],
