{"requirements": [
{"id": "R-SOC", "parent": "SN-1", "value": 3.34, "unit": "%", "basis": "Required gross 2.750+0.089=2.839 MWh against 3.0977 MWh over the window (3.0087+0.089) leaves 8.35% of the 80% window, 6.68% SOC, split over the top and bottom ends, so 3.34% each."},
{"id": "R-TRIP", "parent": "SN-4", "value": 150, "unit": "ms", "basis": "Cell datasheet: above 3.75 V the cell must be disconnected within 150 ms. Chain scan, 4-scan confirmation, MCU cycle and contactor opening must fit inside this."},
{"id": "R-PRE", "parent": "SN-3", "value": 9.5, "unit": "s", "basis": "10 s PCS DC bus ready minus the 0.5 s start sequence before precharge."},
{"id": "R-BAL", "parent": ["SN-1", "SN-4"], "value": 27, "unit": "mA", "basis": "Self-discharge spread at 30 C is about 1.44 %/month (doubling per 10 C). That is 0.048%/day of 224.7 Ah, or 0.108 Ah/day, removed in 4 h/day."},
{"id": "R-BRK", "parent": "SN-4", "value": 2976, "unit": "A", "basis": "Above about 2976 A the 400 A gBat fuse pre-arcs faster than the cell short-time limit. Below it the cell is not protected by the fuse, so the contactor must break up to that current."},
{"id": "R-RIDE", "parent": "SN-6", "value": 1.28, "unit": "s", "basis": "Voltage stays below 50% for 1.30 s (0.15+0.3+0.15 s plus 0.7 s recovery to 50%, in the second dip), minus the 20 ms supply hold-up. The rack 24 V must stay up so the plant stays connected."},
{"id": "R-IMD", "parent": ["SN-4", "SN-6"], "value": 83.4, "unit": "uF", "basis": "All racks and both PCS are one galvanically connected unearthed system: 15x1.54 + 2x30 + 15x2x40 m x 0.26 nF/m = 83.4 uF."}
],
