{"requirements": [
{"id": "R-SOC", "parent": "SN-1", "value": 14.3, "unit": "%", "basis": "Net usable energy 3.6213 MWh plus 0.0724 MWh fixed 1 h auxiliary gives 3.6937 MWh gross. To still deliver 2.300 MWh the window must stay at least 64.2% of 80%. That leaves 28.6% of SOC to lose, split over both window ends, so 14.3% each."},
{"id": "R-TRIP", "parent": "SN-4", "value": 150, "unit": "ms", "basis": "Cell safety limit: disconnect within 150 ms above 3.75 V. The chain is 3 confirming scans plus one missed scan (about 61 ms), one 10 ms MCU cycle and the 30 ms contactor opening, about 101 ms."},
{"id": "R-PRE", "parent": "SN-3", "value": 7, "unit": "s", "basis": "8 s DC-bus-ready limit minus the 1 s start sequence. The resistor must also limit peak current to 30 A (R >= 1343.2/30 = 44.8 ohm) and absorb 0.5*4.8 mF*1343.2^2 = 4.33 kJ."},
{"id": "R-BAL", "parent": "SN-1", "value": 15.3, "unit": "mA", "basis": "Self-discharge spread of 1.66%/month at 35 C of 220.9 Ah is 3.67 Ah. Balancing for 8 h/day over 30 days is 240 h, so 3.67 Ah / 240 h = 15.3 mA."},
{"id": "R-BRK", "parent": ["SN-4", "SN-6"], "value": 2760, "unit": "A", "basis": "Above about 6.9x of the 400 A FU-10 (about 2760 A) the fuse pre-arcing time is shorter than the cell short-time limit, so the fuse protects alone. Below that the contactor must interrupt, and the sensor range must reach the contactor breaking capability."},
{"id": "R-RIDE", "parent": ["SN-2", "SN-6"], "value": 2.21, "unit": "s", "basis": "The double fault sequence keeps voltage below 70% from t=0 to 0.7 s + 1.529 s = 2.229 s (70% is reached 1.529 s after the final breaker opening). Subtracting the 20 ms supply hold-up leaves 2.209 s to be bridged."},
{"id": "R-IMD", "parent": ["SN-4", "SN-6"], "value": 72.4, "unit": "uF", "basis": "Transformerless PCS units on a shared ungrounded winding form one galvanically connected IT system. Its leakage capacitance is 19*1.67 + 4*10 + 19*2*80 m*0.23 nF/m = 31.73 + 40 + 0.70 = 72.4 uF, so one plant IMD is used."}
],
